  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through Sunday)\nIssued at 129 PM CDT Mon Aug 31 2026\n\nThe forecast remains unchanged from the previous package. A hot and \nmostly dry weather pattern is in store throughout the rest of the \nweek. This is thanks to upper-level ridging over the region. Similar \nhigh temperatures each day are forecast in the mid 90s to low 100s \nfor most locations. Spots along the river valleys are forecast to \nrange from 103F to 108F. Lows in the upper 60s to mid 70s can be \nexpected each night. Cannot rule out an isolated storm or two (< \n20%) over the Davis and Guadalupe Mountains every afternoon \nthrough this weekend with continued upslope flow, though sinking \nmotion under the ridge will mainly hinder convective initiation. \nBy Sunday, guidance is in agreement with the upper-level ridge of \nhigh pressure being centered across the Central Plains extending \ninto the Southern High Plains. As a result, easterly flow aloft \ncommences which may lower temperatures a few degrees from previous\ndays. Temperatures are expected to remain above normal, with \nmostly dry conditions continuing into next week. \n\nLamberson",
